---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageTitle from '../components/PageTitle.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
// Venue photos stay as placeholders until permission is confirmed (docs/CONTENT-TODO.md §2).
import Flourish from '../components/Flourish.astro';
import { venueGallery } from '../data/links';
---
<Base title="Accommodations — Breanna & Eric">
  <PageTitle title="Accommodations" />
  <Section>
    <p>We’ve reserved Borgo Laticastelli for the weekend, and we’re planning for our guests to stay with us at the borgo from Thursday through Sunday. Having everyone together in one place is one of the things we’re most excited about.</p>
    <p>Dating back to the 12th century, Laticastelli is a restored Tuscan borgo overlooking the Crete Senesi. Its name is said to mean “the castle where light comes from all sides,” which feels especially fitting for the place where this next chapter begins.</p>
    <p class="gallery"><a class="more" href={venueGallery} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official photo gallery &#8599;&#xFE0E;</a></p>
  </Section>
  <Flourish spaced />
  <Figure bleed src="images/art/borgo-wide.jpg" ratio="21 / 9" label="Venue photo: terrace dining at sunset" />

  <Section wide split flip rows={6}>
    <h2>Your Stay</h2>
    <p>Guests staying at Laticastelli should plan to arrive on Thursday, September 16 and check out on Sunday, September 19. Check-in begins at 3:00 PM on Thursday, and checkout is by noon on Sunday.</p>
    <p>You will not need to reserve a room directly with the hotel. Our wedding planner, Ani, will be helping us coordinate room assignments and stay details for the weekend, and personalized lodging information will be shared with each household.</p>
    <p>Breakfast is included each morning of your stay, and guests will have access to the borgo’s pool and shared spaces throughout the weekend.</p>
    <p>Rooms and suites include modern comforts such as air conditioning, Wi-Fi, private bathrooms, hair dryers, safes, and in-room refreshment facilities.</p>
    <p><em>Your household’s lodging details and RSVP information will be shared privately through Joy.</em></p>
    <Figure narrow wash="left" accent="sage" ratio="2 / 3" label="Placeholder image" />
  </Section>

  <Section wide split rows={2}>
    <h2>Life at the Borgo</h2>
    <p>Laticastelli is tucked into the Tuscan countryside, but the weekend is designed so you can settle in and enjoy the borgo without needing to go anywhere else. Between events, there will be time to enjoy the pool, terraces, views, historic lanes, and gathering spaces around the property.</p>
    <Figure narrow wash="right" accent="peach" ratio="2 / 3" label="Placeholder image" />
  </Section>

  <Section wide split flip rows={2}>
    <h2>Cars &amp; Parking</h2>
    <p>You won’t need a car for the wedding weekend, and if you do choose to drive, complimentary parking is available at the borgo. If you’re extending your time in Tuscany, a car can be a lovely way to reach the smaller hill towns and vineyards that are harder to reach by train.</p>
    <Figure narrow wash="left" accent="sage" ratio="2 / 3" label="Placeholder image" />
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <h2>Navigating the Borgo</h2>
    <p>Laticastelli is a historic borgo with stone lanes, steps, and changes in level. If you have any mobility needs, please let us know so we can work with Ani to plan the most appropriate room and arrangements.</p>
  </Section>
</Base>
